00:13:16,000 --> 00:13:17,500
Oh, I see.

266
00:13:17,670 --> 00:13:21,920
Somebody's afraid of a little competition with the ladies?

267
00:13:22,090 --> 00:13:25,510
Looks like someone is the ladies!

268
00:13:26,130 --> 00:13:29,090
You're just jealous because you couldn't pull this off.

269
00:13:29,300 --> 00:13:33,100
Yeah. Now if you'll excuse me, I have a date.

270
00:13:34,930 --> 00:13:39,480
See? All eyes on me!

271
00:13:44,150 --> 00:13:47,240
We are not signing those papers.

272
00:13:44,150 --> 00:13:47,240
Why not?

273
00:13:47,400 --> 00:13:51,070
It's wrong. They made a mistake. They think we're somebody else.

274
00:13:51,280 --> 00:13:53,790
God works in mysterious ways.

275
00:13:54,660 --> 00:13:56,700
You have gotta stop.

276
00:13:57,250 --> 00:13:58,790
But she liked us.

277
00:13:59,000 --> 00:14:01,790
She likes Doctor Chandler and Reverend Monica.

278
00:14:02,460 --> 00:14:06,050
If you think about it, I'm kind of like a reverend.

279
00:14:06,220 --> 00:14:12,600
I mean, as a chef, I serve God by feeding the hungry and poor.

280
00:14:13,180 --> 00:14:16,270
Your veal chop is 34.95.

281
00:14:17,480 --> 00:14:20,310
Come on, I just... I think we've been given an opportunity.

282
00:14:20,480 --> 00:14:23,480
The mistake's already made. They're writing up the papers now.

283
00:14:23,650 --> 00:14:25,570
But we're not the ones she chose.

284
00:14:25,730 --> 00:14:27,820
How can you feel okay about this?

285
00:14:29,450 --> 00:14:31,320
Because.

286
00:14:31,490 --> 00:14:34,780
We may not be who she thinks we are...

287
00:14:34,950 --> 00:14:37,700
...but no one will ever love that baby more than us.

288
00:14:37,910 --> 00:14:39,370
I know.

289
00:14:37,910 --> 00:14:39,370
I mean, who knows...

290
00:14:39,540 --> 00:14:42,630
...how long it's gonna take for someone else to give us a baby?

291
00:14:42,790 --> 00:14:45,630
What if no one ever picks us?

292
00:14:45,800 --> 00:14:47,210
Oh, honey...

293
00:14:47,380 --> 00:14:48,970
Please?

294
00:14:49,130 --> 00:14:51,630
Please. We are so close.

295
00:14:53,510 --> 00:14:55,890
Monica, I want a baby too.

296
00:14:56,060 --> 00:14:58,350
But this woman is giving away her child.

297
00:14:58,520 --> 00:15:01,390
She deserves to know who it's going to.

298
00:15:08,650 --> 00:15:10,780
Okay. You're right.

299
00:15:12,700 --> 00:15:15,120
So we'll tell the truth.

300
00:15:15,280 --> 00:15:18,790
And who knows, you know? Maybe she'll like us for us.

301
00:15:21,420 --> 00:15:23,290
Maybe she will.

302
00:15:24,080 --> 00:15:26,040
Oh, why couldn't I have been a reverend?

303
00:15:26,210 --> 00:15:28,460
You're Jewish.

304
00:15:29,880 --> 00:15:32,090
Technicality!

305
00:15:37,390 --> 00:15:39,140
Garden salad for the lady.

306
00:15:39,310 --> 00:15:42,600
Oh, that looks great. Good ordering.

307
00:15:39,310 --> 00:15:42,600
Ha-ha-ha.

308
00:15:42,770 --> 00:15:46,650
Seafood platter for the gentleman, and extra fries.

309
00:15:46,820 --> 00:15:48,520
Enjoy.

310
00:15:46,820 --> 00:15:48,520
Ha, ha.

311
00:15:50,110 --> 00:15:52,490
Mm. Those fries look delicious.

312
00:15:52,700 --> 00:15:55,160
Oh, I didn't know you liked french fries.

313
00:15:52,700 --> 00:15:55,160
Ha, ha.

314
00:15:55,320 --> 00:15:57,200
Help yourself. What's mine is yours.

315
00:16:01,540 --> 00:16:04,370
Oh. Wow, are those stuffed clams?

316
00:16:07,880 --> 00:16:08,960
Uh...

317
00:16:09,130 --> 00:16:11,460
Yes, they are my stuffed clams.

318
00:16:13,930 --> 00:16:15,590
How about those fries, though, huh?

319
00:16:17,810 --> 00:16:20,680
They are delicious. Ha-ha-ha.

320
00:16:17,810 --> 00:16:20,680
Yeah.

321
00:16:23,520 --> 00:16:27,020
You are beautiful, you know that?

322
00:16:28,230 --> 00:16:30,110
That is so sweet.

323
00:16:31,820 --> 00:16:34,110
Okay, then.

324
00:16:35,240 --> 00:16:36,700
Mm.

325
00:16:40,120 --> 00:16:41,790
Mm-hm.

326
00:16:45,540 --> 00:16:47,210
Now look what you did!

327
00:16:47,380 --> 00:16:50,040
What? What is the matter with you?

328
00:16:50,250 --> 00:16:53,590
I don't like it when people take food off of my plate, okay?

329
00:16:53,800 --> 00:16:55,760
But you said, "What's mine is yours."

330
00:16:55,970 --> 00:16:57,640
Well, I didn't mean it!

331
00:16:58,970 --> 00:17:03,350
Fine. Sorry, I didn't think it was that big a deal.

332
00:17:04,940 --> 00:17:06,890
No, I'm sorry. I...

333
00:17:07,060 --> 00:17:11,520
I'm overreacting, okay? It's just, when it comes to food, I...

334
00:17:11,690 --> 00:17:13,230
...have certain rules...

335
00:17:13,440 --> 00:17:15,190
...okay? I mean...

336
00:17:15,400 --> 00:17:20,370
...there are things you do, and, you know, things that you don't do.

337
00:17:27,330 --> 00:17:28,790
Wow, this place looks great.

338
00:17:28,960 --> 00:17:33,630
Oh, you are gonna love it. And I'm so glad we're finally doing this.

339
00:17:33,800 --> 00:17:36,840
Me too.

340
00:17:33,800 --> 00:17:36,840
Here.

341
00:17:45,230 --> 00:17:47,690
So this was fun.

342
00:17:55,740 --> 00:17:58,700
I really am sorry about, you know, before.

343
00:17:58,860 --> 00:18:01,490
And I wanna make sure you know I really do like you.

344
00:18:01,700 --> 00:18:04,450
Sure, just not as much as clams.

345
00:18:04,660 --> 00:18:06,410
Well, stuffed clams, ha, ha...

346
00:18:08,420 --> 00:18:10,330
Chocolate torte for the lady.

347
00:18:08,420 --> 00:18:10,330
Mm.

348
00:18:10,500 --> 00:18:12,630
Cheesecake for the gentleman.

349
00:18:12,840 --> 00:18:17,590
Uh, excuse me, sir. There seems to be some sort of red crap on my cheesecake.

350
00:18:18,180 --> 00:18:21,140
Oh. Yes, that's a raspberry coulis.

351
00:18:21,350 --> 00:18:24,850
I'm so stupid ordering cheesecake, trying to be healthy.

352
00:18:26,480 --> 00:18:28,560
Oh, my God. Mm.

353
00:18:28,770 --> 00:18:31,270
I'll just have what she's having.

354
00:18:28,770 --> 00:18:31,270
I'm sorry, sir.

355
00:18:31,440 --> 00:18:33,310
That was our last piece.

356
00:18:31,440 --> 00:18:33,310
Mm.

357
00:18:34,400 --> 00:18:36,230
Mm. Mm.

358
00:18:37,740 --> 00:18:39,780
Oh, no.

359
00:18:39,950 --> 00:18:42,740
This is work. I should call in. Can you excuse me?

360
00:18:42,910 --> 00:18:45,120
Oh, yeah, sure. No problem.

361
00:18:47,450 --> 00:18:50,620
What are you doing? I thought you don't share food?

362
00:18:50,790 --> 00:18:52,250
Sure I do.

363
00:18:52,460 --> 00:18:54,130
Coulis?

364
00:18:52,460 --> 00:18:54,130
Ha, ha.

365
00:18:54,630 --> 00:18:58,630
No. If I can't have your clams, you can't have my dessert.

366
00:18:58,800 --> 00:19:00,260
This is a two-way street.

367
00:19:03,140 --> 00:19:04,680
Really?

368
00:19:05,470 --> 00:19:06,510
Really.

369
00:19:06,680 --> 00:19:09,730
Now this all better be here when I come back.

370
00:19:09,890 --> 00:19:14,940
Yeah, of course. I can control myself. Ha-ha-ha. Yeah.

371
00:19:25,950 --> 00:19:28,330
Stop staring at me!

372
00:19:39,090 --> 00:19:42,130
Just a tiny little... Ha, ha.

373
00:19:44,640 --> 00:19:46,640
Uh-oh.

374
00:19:56,110 --> 00:19:58,650
I'm not even sorry.

375
00:20:02,570 --> 00:20:04,740
Hi.

376
00:20:02,570 --> 00:20:04,740
Hey.

377
00:20:04,910 --> 00:20:08,830
So these are the preliminary forms for an open adoption. Uh...

378
00:20:09,040 --> 00:20:11,910
There's a lot to go over, but I'll explain as we go through.

379
00:20:12,750 --> 00:20:16,170
Is that a picture?

380
00:20:12,750 --> 00:20:16,170
Yeah.

381
00:20:16,380 --> 00:20:18,840
It's a sonogram they took of the baby last week.

382
00:20:19,000 --> 00:20:20,670
I thought you might wanna see it.

383
00:20:28,220 --> 00:20:30,220
Look, doctor.

384
00:20:34,270 --> 00:20:37,520
Look, before we sign anything, we really have to talk.

385
00:20:41,030 --> 00:20:42,900
We're not who you think we are.

386
00:20:43,070 --> 00:20:46,200
I don't understand.

387
00:20:43,070 --> 00:20:46,200
The agency must have made a mistake.

388
00:20:46,370 --> 00:20:49,280
My wife is not a reverend, and I'm not a doctor.

389
00:20:49,490 --> 00:20:51,370
What?

390
00:20:49,490 --> 00:20:51,370
That's impossible.

391
00:20:51,580 --> 00:20:54,910
I could perform an operation on you and prove it if you'd like.

392
00:20:56,670 --> 00:20:59,840
Um, I have to check your file. Excuse me.

393
00:21:00,000 --> 00:21:01,300
So who are you?

394
00:21:01,510 --> 00:21:04,590
Our names really are Monica and Chandler. We're from New York.

395
00:21:04,760 --> 00:21:07,180
Yeah, but the important thing to know about us...

396
00:21:07,340 --> 00:21:10,510
...is how much we would care for this little baby.

397
00:21:10,720 --> 00:21:12,720
So you lied to me before?

398
00:21:12,890 --> 00:21:16,480
Well, we "bore false witness."

399
00:21:17,900 --> 00:21:20,400
See? I could be a reverend.

400
00:21:21,400 --> 00:21:22,980
I can't believe this.

401
00:21:23,150 --> 00:21:25,740
But we were hoping that since we told you the truth...

402
00:21:25,900 --> 00:21:28,950
...that you still might consider...

403
00:21:25,900 --> 00:21:28,950
Giving you my baby?

404
00:21:29,120 --> 00:21:31,240
You think I'd give you my child after this?

405
00:21:31,450 --> 00:21:34,080
You don't have to decide now. If you look at our file...

406
00:21:34,250 --> 00:21:37,330
I don't wanna look at your file. This is over.

407
00:21:41,750 --> 00:21:43,500
Erica, wait.

408
00:21:43,670 --> 00:21:45,630
I have nothing to say to you.

409
00:21:45,800 --> 00:21:49,550
Look, you have every reason to be upset. We did lie.

410
00:21:49,760 --> 00:21:53,810
But only because we've been waiting and trying to have a baby for so long.

411
00:21:53,970 --> 00:21:57,440
And we don't know how long it's gonna be before we get another chance.

412
00:21:57,640 --> 00:21:59,810
Why don't you ask the reverend to pray on it?

413
00:21:59,980 --> 00:22:02,480
Erica, please.

414
00:22:03,070 --> 00:22:07,190
Just consider us. Ask them to see our file.

415
00:22:07,360 --> 00:22:09,320
Our last name's Bing.

416
00:22:09,490 --> 00:22:12,070
My wife's a chef and I'm in advertising.

417
00:22:13,160 --> 00:22:14,990
Oh, yeah.

418
00:22:15,160 --> 00:22:17,710
I actually liked you guys.

419
00:22:19,170 --> 00:22:21,460
But it doesn't matter. What you did was wrong.

420
00:22:21,630 --> 00:22:24,250
But you did like us.

421
00:22:24,420 --> 00:22:26,260
And you should.

422
00:22:26,760 --> 00:22:29,010
My wife's an incredible woman.

423
00:22:29,180 --> 00:22:33,220
She is loving, and devoted and caring.

424
00:22:33,640 --> 00:22:37,560
And don't tell her I said this, but the woman's always right.

425
00:22:41,270 --> 00:22:44,770
I love my wife more than anything in this world.

426
00:22:46,070 --> 00:22:47,650
And it...

427
00:22:48,780 --> 00:22:52,240
It kills me that I can't give her a baby.

428
00:22:57,620 --> 00:23:00,000
I really want a kid.

429
00:23:01,080 --> 00:23:04,790
And when that day finally comes, I'll learn how to be a good dad.

430
00:23:05,380 --> 00:23:07,300
But my wife...

431
00:23:07,630 --> 00:23:09,760
...she's already there.

432
00:23:10,090 --> 00:23:12,090
She's a mother...

433
00:23:13,180 --> 00:23:15,220
...without a baby.

434
00:23:22,400 --> 00:23:24,190
Please?

435
00:23:36,030 --> 00:23:38,160
You still want that baby?

436
00:23:53,800 --> 00:23:56,010
God bless you, Chandler Bing!

437
00:24:09,900 --> 00:24:12,530
Turns out this sweater is made for a woman.

438
00:24:14,910 --> 00:24:16,910
So why are you still wearing it?

439
00:24:17,120 --> 00:24:18,660
Because it's soft.

440
00:24:20,700 --> 00:24:22,250
Hey, so how was your date?

441
00:24:20,700 --> 00:24:22,250
Ugh.

442
00:24:22,460 --> 00:24:24,250
Not so good.

443
00:24:26,040 --> 00:24:30,590
Well, looks like it's just the two of us tonight, huh, buddy?

444
00:24:30,760 --> 00:24:33,800
Yeah. And you know what? We could do a lot worse.

445
00:24:33,970 --> 00:24:36,890
Yeah.

446
00:24:33,970 --> 00:24:36,890
Yeah. Ha-ha-ha.

447
00:24:38,180 --> 00:24:41,180
Joey doesn't share food!

